{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Tracker(store:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A store keeps only the event types you list in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"date in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Date?]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type of your own or in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types are delivered in this run but never written.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each drop is reported on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"reference"},{"text":" as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"reference"},{"text":": the oldest segments","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at another ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schemaVersion"},{"text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"text":" set. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","type":"reference"},{"text":", after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DatabaseStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRDBPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self], directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"Persistence","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"Persistence"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"anchor":"Stores"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"]}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"title":"SegmentStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"title":"dropReports","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"synchronize"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"synchronize()"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure."}],"title":"SegmentStoreError","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"link","title":"Persisting Records","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persisting Records"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A store keeping events of the types ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"directory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; it recovers the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already there.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"events","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [any (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP","text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Co